---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { responsible } from '../../data/legal';
---
<LegalLayout title="Terms of use" description="The terms for using the Bracket Systems website: acceptable use, intellectual property, liability and changes.">
  <h2>About these terms</h2>
  <p>These terms cover your use of this website. They don't cover HR &amp; Payroll licenses or custom development
  projects — those are agreed separately, in writing, with each customer.</p>

  <h2>Using the site</h2>
  <p>You may browse the site and share its pages. Please don't try to disrupt it, get around its security, overload the
  contact form, or use it to send spam or unlawful content.</p>

  <h2>Accounts</h2>
  <p>The site has no user accounts. There's no public live instance of HR &amp; Payroll here, and none of our demos
  should be used with real personal data.</p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>The text, design, logo and product screenshots on this site belong to Bracket Systems' developers. The product
  screenshots show a fictional company; names and figures in them are made up. Client names are shown with reference to
  work we did for them and don't imply their endorsement.</p>

  <h2>Information on this site</h2>
  <p>We work to describe our product and services accurately, and we mark features that are planned or API-only. Even
  so, the site is provided for information: features, editions and availability can change, and a quote or written
  agreement is what defines what you get. Payroll and tax rules change too; have your accountant check any configuration.</p>

  <h2>Service availability</h2>
  <p>We aim to keep the site available but don't guarantee it will be uninterrupted or error-free.</p>

  <h2>Third-party services and links</h2>
  <p>The site relies on providers listed in the <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a> and links to other sites
  (such as LinkedIn). We're not responsible for their content or practices.</p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>To the extent the law allows, we're not liable for indirect or consequential loss arising from use of this website.
  Nothing in these terms limits liability that can't be limited by law.</p>

  <h2>Ending access</h2>
  <p>We may block access for anyone who misuses the site, for example by abusing the contact form.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms; the date at the top shows the latest version.</p>

  <h2>Governing law and contact</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Philippines. Questions: {responsible.map((r, i) => <>{i > 0 && ', '}<a href={`mailto:${r.email}`}>{r.email}</a></>)}.</p>
</LegalLayout>
